.KEY DIR/A,STEP/K
.BRA {
.KET }
; Python3 install: Python 3.14 in SYS:Python3, with the ixemul.library it runs on
; It stands alone: nothing here needs UP-Term, and nothing here looks at an UP-Term:
; assign (that would ask for the volume).
; Run by this archive's Install (an Installer script), which asks the questions:
;   Execute <archive>/Files/install.dos <archive>/Files [STEP <part>]
; From a Shell without Installer the same line installs everything. The Installer
; runs the parts one at a time with STEP (tests/test_dist_addons.py holds the two to
; the same list); the first part, check, has nothing to check for a stand-alone archive.
FailAt 21
; the archive's Files drawer: every name below is relative to it
CD "{DIR}"
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Skip {STEP}
EndIf
; @include dist/common/@CHECKFRAG@
Lab ixemul
; Python needs ixemul.library 47 or newer. A library of that version or newer that is
; already in LIBS: stays as it is: never a downgrade, and never over UP-Term's patched
; ixemul.library (version 80), which Python then uses. Only when there is none that new
; this archive's ixemul.library 80.1 goes in, with the ixnet.library of the same build
; (ixnet refuses an ixemul of another revision); an older one is kept as
; <name>.before-Python3 and put back by Uninstall. ENVARC:uppkg/ixemul records it: the
; marker installed-by-Python3 says this archive put the library there, and needs/<archive>
; says who needs it (Uninstall removes the library only when nobody else does).
MakeDir >NIL: ENVARC:uppkg ENVARC:uppkg/ixemul ENVARC:uppkg/ixemul/needs
Version >NIL: LIBS:ixemul.library 47
If WARN
  If EXISTS LIBS:ixemul.library
    Copy LIBS:ixemul.library LIBS:ixemul.library.before-Python3 CLONE QUIET
  EndIf
  If EXISTS LIBS:ixnet.library
    Copy LIBS:ixnet.library LIBS:ixnet.library.before-Python3 CLONE QUIET
  EndIf
  Copy libs/ixemul.library LIBS:ixemul.library CLONE QUIET
  Copy libs/ixnet.library LIBS:ixnet.library CLONE QUIET
  Echo >ENVARC:uppkg/ixemul/installed-by-Python3 "Python3.lha put ixemul.library and ixnet.library in LIBS:"
EndIf
Echo >ENVARC:uppkg/ixemul/needs/Python3 "Python3"
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Quit 0
EndIf
Lab copy-python
; Python 3.14 (README): SYS:Python3, its programs run as Python3:bin/python3 (the assign,
; the next part) or SYS:Python3/bin/python3; vsh's path names /SYS/Python3/bin.
MakeDir >NIL: SYS:Python3
Copy python3 SYS:Python3 ALL CLONE QUIET
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Quit 0
EndIf
Lab python
; Python3: assigned now and at every boot: a block in S:User-Startup that assigns only while
; SYS:Python3 is there, so one left behind by an Uninstall that could not take it out does no
; harm. S:User-Startup as it was is kept (record drawer) for Uninstall to put back.
Assign Python3: SYS:Python3
Search >NIL: S:User-Startup ";BEGIN Python3"
If WARN
  MakeDir >NIL: ENVARC:uppkg ENVARC:uppkg/Python3
  Copy S:User-Startup ENVARC:uppkg/Python3/User-Startup.before CLONE QUIET
  Echo >>S:User-Startup ";BEGIN Python3"
  Echo >>S:User-Startup "If EXISTS SYS:Python3"
  Echo >>S:User-Startup "  Assign Python3: SYS:Python3"
  Echo >>S:User-Startup "EndIf"
  Echo >>S:User-Startup ";END Python3"
EndIf
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Quit 0
EndIf
; @include dist/common/record.dos
Echo "Python3 installed: Python3:bin/python3 (in an UP-Term window: python3)."
